  "id": "expert-power",
  "term": "expert power",
  "definition": "Expert power is a form of influence that comes from being seen as knowledgeable or highly skilled in a relevant area. In this source, it refers to consultants’ ability to affect clients through their expertise, which was linked to stronger client self-efficacy, although this link was weaker when managerial stress was high.",
